MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache feels like the strongest next choice because its heavy riffs and strong melodies match what draws me to In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Lost and Found, With Teeth, and Mezmerize fit my current interest in aggression with melody, texture, or unexpected turns, alongside my recent Disturbed and Tool listening. City of Evil also connects with the fast riffs and hooks I enjoyed in Advance And Vanquish."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Airbag/How Am I Driving? feels less appealing for this session because I want a heavier sound; a connection to my broader rock listening does not meet that immediate preference.",
    "Elements 1 takes the heaviness toward power metal, while Divine Intervention offers more relentless thrash than I want today. Neither hits the balance of weight, groove, and melody that makes The End of Heartache appealing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated as a reason to expect equal interest in power metal, thrash, and melodic heavy music, although those sounds satisfy different moods for me.",
    "A broad connection to alternative rock seems to count too much when I am currently drawn to heavier riffs and a stronger sense of impact."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of heaviness and memorable melody matters more to me right now than intensity alone, especially given my repeated listening to In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Something can fit my taste without being an immediate choice: Someone In Control and Point #1 interest me, but the other albums offer a more compelling match for this session."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations largely understand my interest in heavy rock and metal, but sometimes miss the particular balance of melody, groove, and intensity I want right now."
}
